<!-- @after Mental Model :: visual -->
### Three ways the same method can run

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-cols" style="--cols:3"><div class="col"><span class="col-title">Interpreted</span><div class="node"><strong>When</strong><small>no compiled code exists yet for the method</small></div><div class="node" data-state="warn"><strong>Cost</strong><small>slowest per call, nothing to compile first</small></div></div><div class="col"><span class="col-title">JIT</span><div class="node"><strong>When</strong><small>a method turns hot while the app runs</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Leaves behind</strong><small>a profile file listing the hot code</small></div></div><div class="col"><span class="col-title">AOT (speed-profile)</span><div class="node is-key"><strong>When</strong><small>at install from a cloud profile, or when the device is idle and charging</small></div><div class="node is-key"><strong>Leaves behind</strong><small>an <code>.oat</code> file of compiled methods</small></div></div></div><figcaption>The profile is the link between the columns: JIT records what ran, and dex2oat compiles those methods ahead of time for later launches.</figcaption></figure>

